    <statement><p>Let <m>\vec F(x,y,z) = 4x^2\vec i - \cos(xy)(\vec i + \vec j)</m>.
Calculate the divergence:</p>
<p><m>\mbox{div }\vec F(x,y,z) =</m> <fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>2\cdot 4x+y\sin\mathopen{}\left(xy\right)+x\sin\mathopen{}\left(xy\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><me>\mbox{div } (4x^2\vec i - \cos(xy)(\vec i + \vec j)) = 8x+y\sin\mathopen{}\left(xy\right)+x\sin\mathopen{}\left(xy\right).</me>




</solution>
